1
00:00:00,140 --> 00:00:02,520
Greetings, fellow aliens!

2
00:00:02,520 --> 00:00:40,210
Today we will talk about one of the earthlings'
favourite things: Food.

3
00:00:40,210 --> 00:00:45,539
Like many organisms, earthlings need various
chemicals to sustain their metabolism.

4
00:00:45,539 --> 00:00:47,969
These chemicals are taken in three ways:

5
00:00:47,969 --> 00:00:50,680
Breathing, drinking and eating.

6
00:00:50,680 --> 00:00:56,359
Breathing means aspirating oxygen and exhaling
carbon dioxide, which is heavier than oxygen.

7
00:00:56,359 --> 00:01:01,280
So, earthlings loose constantly weight through
breathing, approximately half a kilogram per

8
00:01:01,280 --> 00:01:06,180
day, which is of course replaced by eating
and drinking.

9
00:01:06,180 --> 00:01:08,730
Eating means taking ailments through the mouth.

10
00:01:08,730 --> 00:01:13,210
The mouth has two purposes: Shredding the
food, and analyzing it.

11
00:01:13,210 --> 00:01:18,100
Drinking is basically the same, but with liquids
- mainly hydric acid.

12
00:01:18,100 --> 00:01:22,220
Besides hydric acid, there are three main
components of food:

13
00:01:22,220 --> 00:01:26,140
Carbohydrates, fat and proteins.

14
00:01:26,140 --> 00:01:28,340
Carbohydrates are the main energy source of
the body.

15
00:01:28,340 --> 00:01:33,210
Remember sugar, the energy-rich molecules
produced by plants out of sunlight and thin

16
00:01:33,210 --> 00:01:34,210
air?

17
00:01:34,210 --> 00:01:38,380
The simplest sugars are glucose, fructose
and sucrose.

18
00:01:38,380 --> 00:01:41,350
Glucose looks a bit like a Centauri donut
with a little flag,

19
00:01:41,350 --> 00:01:44,040
fructose like a smaller donut with two little
flags,

20
00:01:44,040 --> 00:01:46,719
and sucrose like the two of them glued together.

21
00:01:46,719 --> 00:01:50,719
There are also non-circular variants of those
molecules.

22
00:01:50,719 --> 00:01:56,170
Now, carbohydrates are basically sugar, and
everything you can assemble from sugar.

23
00:01:56,170 --> 00:02:00,789
For example, when you create a glucose chain
and put all the little flags in the same direction,

24
00:02:00,789 --> 00:02:06,250
you get starch, a good energy source - you
find it, for example, in bread.

25
00:02:06,250 --> 00:02:11,400
But when you alternate the orientation of
the flags, you get cellulose, which is indigestible

26
00:02:11,400 --> 00:02:13,440
for earth creatures.

27
00:02:13,440 --> 00:02:18,500
Except for the microbes.

28
00:02:18,500 --> 00:02:22,600
Even cellulose-eating animals like cows can't
digest it by themselves;

29
00:02:22,600 --> 00:02:25,760
they have it digested by microbes in their
bowels.

30
00:02:25,760 --> 00:02:28,870
A special kind of cellulose structure is wood
-

31
00:02:28,870 --> 00:02:31,440
the stuff the stems of trees are made of.

32
00:02:31,440 --> 00:02:35,370
It's basically cellulose fibers held together
by a matrix of lignin.

33
00:02:35,370 --> 00:02:39,680
Wood is not edible either, but it plays an
important part in the development of earthling

34
00:02:39,680 --> 00:02:40,769
alimentation.

35
00:02:40,769 --> 00:02:43,010
We will come back to this later.

36
00:02:43,010 --> 00:02:46,489
The second component of earthling food are
fats.

37
00:02:46,489 --> 00:02:47,489
What is fat?

38
00:02:47,489 --> 00:02:51,400
Well, fat molecules look a bit like fat little
baby squids,

39
00:02:51,400 --> 00:02:54,970
with a body of glycerol and three tentacles
of fatty acids.

40
00:02:54,970 --> 00:02:58,190
Missing hydrogen atoms in the tentacles create
kinks,

41
00:02:58,190 --> 00:03:01,670
in this case we speak of unsaturated fatty
acids.

42
00:03:01,670 --> 00:03:05,080
Anyway, creatures use fat principally to store
energy,

43
00:03:05,080 --> 00:03:08,420
for example to survive the cold season when
food is rare.

44
00:03:08,420 --> 00:03:13,409
Predators, and earthlings in particular, love
eating fat of other creatures.

45
00:03:13,409 --> 00:03:17,659
In rich countries, people have nowadays so
much to eat that they often accumulate too

46
00:03:17,659 --> 00:03:18,959
much fat.

47
00:03:18,959 --> 00:03:24,080
They try to burn fat with physical exercises
- when the body burns fat, it produces more

48
00:03:24,080 --> 00:03:26,920
carbon dioxide, thus loses more weight.

49
00:03:26,920 --> 00:03:31,299
A less exhausting way of burning fat would
probably be to simply turn the heating down

50
00:03:31,299 --> 00:03:36,220
- when it's cold, the earthling body consumes
energy to maintain its temperature.

51
00:03:36,220 --> 00:03:40,810
Strangely, this method is not very popular.

52
00:03:40,810 --> 00:03:42,410
The third component of food are proteins.

53
00:03:42,410 --> 00:03:43,410
What is a protein?

54
00:03:43,410 --> 00:03:51,409
Well, proteins are incredibly complex molecules
which are basically the backbone of the metabolism.

55
00:03:51,409 --> 00:03:55,450
An important kinds of proteins is those little
nanobots called enzymes which basically run

56
00:03:55,450 --> 00:03:56,530
the organism on a molecular level.

57
00:03:56,530 --> 00:04:02,090
If the organism was a factory, enzymes would
be the robot workers.

58
00:04:02,090 --> 00:04:06,459
The blueprints for these protein-nanobots
are all encoded in the DNA.

59
00:04:06,459 --> 00:04:11,460
But how can a one-dimensional genetic code
contain blueprints of three-dimensional nanomachines?

60
00:04:11,460 --> 00:04:17,410
Well, all proteins are made of only twenty
basic building blocks called amino acids.

61
00:04:17,410 --> 00:04:21,200
Those building blocks can be plugged together
to build long chains.

62
00:04:21,200 --> 00:04:23,300
That's exactly how proteins are build:

63
00:04:23,300 --> 00:04:28,510
The DNA sequences are translated into amino
acid chains, with three base pairs corresponding

64
00:04:28,510 --> 00:04:30,630
to one type of amino acid.

65
00:04:30,630 --> 00:04:35,570
Once the chain is built, it naturally curls
together to some wibbly wobbly curly whirly

66
00:04:35,570 --> 00:04:38,030
thing, the actual protein.

67
00:04:38,030 --> 00:04:42,891
Now, some of these basic building blocks can't
be synthesized by the earthling body, they

68
00:04:42,891 --> 00:04:45,130
need to be taken from plants and animals -

69
00:04:45,130 --> 00:04:50,470
either by eating protein packages they produce
for their offspring, or by eating their body,

70
00:04:50,470 --> 00:04:52,290
especially muscle tissue.

71
00:04:52,290 --> 00:04:57,520
Those building blocks are called essential
amino acids.

72
00:04:57,520 --> 00:05:00,220
Strategic advice.

73
00:05:00,220 --> 00:05:04,950
Earthlings eat a lot of meat, and most of
the meet comes from tamed animals like cows.

74
00:05:04,950 --> 00:05:09,950
So you might have the idea of weakening earthlings
with a massive abduction of cows.

75
00:05:09,950 --> 00:05:13,710
However, this tactic might backfire on the
long run :

76
00:05:13,710 --> 00:05:18,490
Many earthlings nutritionists and ecologists
think that modern earthlings eat far too much

77
00:05:18,490 --> 00:05:21,940
meat, especially in rich countries.

78
00:05:21,940 --> 00:05:29,350
So, when you abduct most of the cows, you
might actually do mankind a favour.

79
00:05:29,350 --> 00:05:34,940
Besides hydric acid, carbohydrates, fat and
proteins, earthlings need other things in

80
00:05:34,940 --> 00:05:42,930
smaller quantities, for example iron, calcium,
vitamins and sodium chloride, aka salt.

81
00:05:42,930 --> 00:05:44,300
Salt is an ionic compound,

82
00:05:44,300 --> 00:05:47,400
hold together not by an electron sharing deal,

83
00:05:47,400 --> 00:05:49,150
but an electron lending deal.

84
00:05:49,150 --> 00:05:54,550
A sodium atom lends an electron to a chlorine
atom, so they have both a complete outer shell.

85
00:05:54,550 --> 00:06:00,100
This makes both atoms electrically charged,
in other words ions, so they stick together.

86
00:06:00,100 --> 00:06:02,210
This is called an ionic bond.

87
00:06:02,210 --> 00:06:05,620
Salt is very important for the earthling metabolism.

88
00:06:05,620 --> 00:06:09,590
Some food, on the other side, is dangerous
for the body.

89
00:06:09,590 --> 00:06:14,380
This holds particularly for food infested
or altered by tiny food rivals or parasites

90
00:06:14,380 --> 00:06:17,370
like microbes, insects or fungi.

91
00:06:17,370 --> 00:06:18,960
This kind of food is called rotten.

92
00:06:18,960 --> 00:06:24,990
To distinguish good food from bad or rotten
food, earthlings need a way to analyze food

93
00:06:24,990 --> 00:06:26,620
before eating it.

94
00:06:26,620 --> 00:06:28,850
That's the purpose of smell and taste.

95
00:06:28,850 --> 00:06:33,750
The nose and the mouth contain arrays of chemical
sensors called chemo-receptors which are linked

96
00:06:33,750 --> 00:06:35,580
to the brain's reward system.

97
00:06:35,580 --> 00:06:41,010
Basically, "good" food causes pleasure and
the urge to swallow, "bad" food creates displeasure

98
00:06:41,010 --> 00:06:43,670
and the urge to spit it out.

99
00:06:43,670 --> 00:06:47,760
The pleasure is also modified depending on
the current needs of the body - after eating

100
00:06:47,760 --> 00:06:52,690
six animal bodies, the seventh one just doesn't
taste so good anymore.

101
00:06:52,690 --> 00:06:57,710
Also, finding food pleasurable can be learned
- many earthlings have learned to appreciate

102
00:06:57,710 --> 00:06:59,920
rotten food like cheese or beer.

103
00:06:59,920 --> 00:07:02,100
We will come back to this in a moment.

104
00:07:02,100 --> 00:07:05,960
Food appreciation is so transmitted from generation
to generation.

105
00:07:05,960 --> 00:07:08,230
This is called food culture.

106
00:07:08,230 --> 00:07:14,670
There are basically five kinds of taste: sweet,
sour, salty, bitter and umami.

107
00:07:14,670 --> 00:07:19,290
Sweet is the simplest one, a pleasing sensation
which indicates the earthlings prefered energy

108
00:07:19,290 --> 00:07:21,520
source: sugar.

109
00:07:21,520 --> 00:07:27,610
Sour indicates acids like citric acid or Vitamin
C, which you find in many fruits.

110
00:07:27,610 --> 00:07:33,900
Salty indicates primarily the presence of
sodium ions, in particular from sodium chloride.

111
00:07:33,900 --> 00:07:38,720
Bitter is a generally displeasing, alarming
taste which may hint at rotten or poisonous

112
00:07:38,720 --> 00:07:39,820
food.

113
00:07:39,820 --> 00:07:44,200
The last one, umami, indicates a compound
called glutamate.

114
00:07:44,200 --> 00:07:48,410
It can be found in many types of food and
is generally perceived as savoury.

115
00:07:48,410 --> 00:07:54,050
There might be a sixth taste, which indicates
fat, but for now that's just a hypothesis.

116
00:07:54,050 --> 00:07:57,950
Interestingly, some food acts not on the taste
receptors but on the temperature receptors

117
00:07:57,950 --> 00:07:58,950
in the mouth:

118
00:07:58,950 --> 00:08:02,170
Mint oil, for example, is perceived as cool,

119
00:08:02,170 --> 00:08:06,630
whereas so-called "spicy" food triggers the
heat receptors and may even be perceived as

120
00:08:06,630 --> 00:08:07,630
painful.

121
00:08:07,630 --> 00:08:10,130
There is a common misconception about taste
:

122
00:08:10,130 --> 00:08:13,750
Many earthlings believe that receptors for
different tastes are located in different

123
00:08:13,750 --> 00:08:15,460
zones of the tongue.

124
00:08:15,460 --> 00:08:20,410
This is easy to disprove, especially for earthlings
- just put something sweet onto the back of

125
00:08:20,410 --> 00:08:23,390
your tongue, or something bitter onto the
tip.

126
00:08:23,390 --> 00:08:27,850
Nevertheless, many earthlings keep on believing
this nonsense rather than trying it out for

127
00:08:27,850 --> 00:08:28,950
themselves.

128
00:08:28,950 --> 00:08:32,800
Now, where do the earthlings get all the edible
stuff?

129
00:08:32,800 --> 00:08:36,890
At dawn of mankind, they got it essentially
the same way as animals :

130
00:08:36,890 --> 00:08:41,979
By hunting animals and gathering fruits and
seeds, and devouring the edible parts.

131
00:08:41,979 --> 00:08:47,260
But at some point, they made an important
discovery: Artificial external digestion.

132
00:08:47,260 --> 00:08:50,540
This is similar to methods used by other races
in the galaxy.

133
00:08:50,540 --> 00:08:55,460
The Snuglings of Karaxi-2, for example, live
under a thick cloud cover protecting them

134
00:08:55,460 --> 00:08:57,910
from the deadly radiation of their sun.

135
00:08:57,910 --> 00:09:02,200
They feed on creatures called frooks, but
some kinds of Frooks are hard to kill and

136
00:09:02,200 --> 00:09:03,830
difficult to digest.

137
00:09:03,830 --> 00:09:07,710
So the Snuglings catapult the frooks above
the cloud cover where they are roasted by

138
00:09:07,710 --> 00:09:09,760
the gamma rays of the sun.

139
00:09:09,760 --> 00:09:15,260
When they fall down, they are easier to digest,
and also, dead.

140
00:09:15,260 --> 00:09:24,000
Some 400000 solar cycles ago, Earthlings discovered
a similar method to make food digestible : Fire!

141
00:09:24,000 --> 00:09:27,210
Remember wood, this hardened cellulose structure
?

142
00:09:27,210 --> 00:09:32,100
Dry wood combusts easily, and it's not hard
to build a fire out of wood pieces.

143
00:09:32,100 --> 00:09:38,630
Originally, earthlings used fire to keep warm
and drive away predators, but some 250000

144
00:09:38,630 --> 00:09:43,560
solar cycles ago they discovered that some
food, in particular meat, changes its taste

145
00:09:43,560 --> 00:09:46,940
and consistency when exposed to fire for a
while.

146
00:09:46,940 --> 00:09:49,320
This is called roasting.

147
00:09:49,320 --> 00:09:51,200
But why do earthlings do that?

148
00:09:51,200 --> 00:09:54,320
Well, there are several reasons for roasting.

149
00:09:54,320 --> 00:09:58,050
First, the heat kills most of the microbes
in the food.

150
00:09:58,050 --> 00:10:03,240
Secondly, the temperature breaks down molecules
like starch and unfolds some proteins, which

151
00:10:03,240 --> 00:10:06,180
makes the food easier to chew and easier to
digest.

152
00:10:06,180 --> 00:10:11,450
Basically, roasting food is some kind of external
pre-digestion, using the chemical energy in

153
00:10:11,450 --> 00:10:12,530
wood.

154
00:10:12,530 --> 00:10:17,380
Now, when roasting food, it often gets a brown
crispy crust.

155
00:10:17,380 --> 00:10:20,280
What happens here is called "Maillard reaction".

156
00:10:20,280 --> 00:10:24,310
Basically, it's a reaction between sugar and
amino acids.

157
00:10:24,310 --> 00:10:26,310
Earthlings love the taste of this crust.

158
00:10:26,310 --> 00:10:32,230
By the way, many earthlings think that roasting
meat "seals in the juices" - but that is nonsense.

159
00:10:32,230 --> 00:10:38,300
Now, another way of heating food is boiling
it - exposing it to boiling hydric acid.

160
00:10:38,300 --> 00:10:41,670
Boiling differs from roasting in that the
temperature doesn't exceed the boiling point

161
00:10:41,670 --> 00:10:45,220
of hydric acid, and there is no Maillard reaction.

162
00:10:45,220 --> 00:10:50,960
Basically, it's just another variant of the
same external pre-digestion process.

163
00:10:50,960 --> 00:10:56,000
Boiling and roasting are part of what earthlings
do with their food before they eat it: Cooking.

164
00:10:56,000 --> 00:10:59,660
And earthlings wouldn't be earthlings if they
hadn't developed cooking into an elaborate

165
00:10:59,660 --> 00:11:01,440
part of their culture.

166
00:11:01,440 --> 00:11:06,820
Cooking also includes cutting and slicing
food, mixing and combining different ingredients,

167
00:11:06,820 --> 00:11:09,050
and spicing the food.

168
00:11:09,050 --> 00:11:13,070
Spicing means adding ingredients that alter
the taste, mostly to increase the pleasure

169
00:11:13,070 --> 00:11:17,670
of eating: Yet another example of earthlings
tricking out their brains' reward system to

170
00:11:17,670 --> 00:11:20,890
get biologically pointless pleasure.

171
00:11:20,890 --> 00:11:22,030
Tips for tourists.

172
00:11:22,030 --> 00:11:26,430
If you have a hydrocarbon-based metabolism,
you might visit a restaurant.

173
00:11:26,430 --> 00:11:29,520
Here you can observe earthlings' eating habits,

174
00:11:29,520 --> 00:11:32,150
and also taste some food for yourself.

175
00:11:32,150 --> 00:11:37,030
However, beware of earthling drinks, they
have often surprising effects.

176
00:11:37,030 --> 00:11:42,180
Some 10000 solar cycles ago, a second discovery
was made :

177
00:11:42,180 --> 00:11:46,760
Earthlings all over the planet started cultivating
food and herding animals.

178
00:11:46,760 --> 00:11:52,040
Basically, they started acting like small-scale
bio administrators, rearing new species of

179
00:11:52,040 --> 00:11:54,860
plants and animals according to their needs.

180
00:11:54,860 --> 00:11:56,870
This is called agriculture.

181
00:11:56,870 --> 00:12:01,100
Nowadays it has grown to an industrial scale
food production able to feed seven billion

182
00:12:01,100 --> 00:12:02,160
earthlings.

183
00:12:02,160 --> 00:12:04,290
Well, almost.

184
00:12:04,290 --> 00:12:08,430
One of the strangest aspects of food culture
is the earthling habit of letting food rot

185
00:12:08,430 --> 00:12:10,060
in a controlled manner.

186
00:12:10,060 --> 00:12:13,310
One example is alcoholic beverages like wine
or beer.

187
00:12:13,310 --> 00:12:18,400
Wine, for example, is rotten juice from fruits
called grapes.

188
00:12:18,400 --> 00:12:21,940
Alcoholic beverages have a particular effect
on the brain - we will talk about this in

189
00:12:21,940 --> 00:12:24,200
another episode.

190
00:12:24,200 --> 00:12:28,030
Another example for deliberately rotten food
are products like yoghurt or cheese :

191
00:12:28,030 --> 00:12:32,780
Milk, altered by microbes, a process that
can take months.

192
00:12:32,780 --> 00:12:36,730
Cheese is sometimes even exposed to fungi
which make it rot even more.

193
00:12:36,730 --> 00:12:41,600
This process transforms the simple taste of
milk into a more complex taste, sometimes

194
00:12:41,600 --> 00:12:43,910
even with hints of bitterness.

195
00:12:43,910 --> 00:12:49,630
Generally, eating is a highly ritualized,
social activity: Social groups eat together,

196
00:12:49,630 --> 00:12:54,021
friends bond by sharing a meal, and mating
rituals often involve eating together in a

197
00:12:54,021 --> 00:12:56,290
public place.

198
00:12:56,290 --> 00:13:01,390
But despite the sophisticated rituals, earthlings
still keep some habits from their cave-dwelling

199
00:13:01,390 --> 00:13:02,390
ancestors.

200
00:13:02,390 --> 00:13:06,950
I have observed several earthling families
where the mother cooks, but calls the father

201
00:13:06,950 --> 00:13:08,190
to cut the roast -

202
00:13:08,190 --> 00:13:11,790
in prehistoric times, the job of the tribe
chieftain.

203
00:13:11,790 --> 00:13:16,910
Also, many men like to roast meat over open
fire, just like mammoth hunters in the olden

204
00:13:16,910 --> 00:13:18,610
days.

205
00:13:18,610 --> 00:13:23,570
Strangely, earthlings often separate "sweet"
sugar snacks from larger "salty" meals which

206
00:13:23,570 --> 00:13:26,320
contain all kinds of nutrients.

207
00:13:26,320 --> 00:13:29,440
The reason might be that both meals have different
functions:

208
00:13:29,440 --> 00:13:33,870
The sugar snacks give a quick energy boost,
which is often enhanced by stimulating drugs

209
00:13:33,870 --> 00:13:37,090
like coffee or cigarettes..

210
00:13:37,090 --> 00:13:43,180
The salty meals, on the other hand, provide
long-term supply with all kinds of nutrients.

211
00:13:43,180 --> 00:13:48,150
Sometimes, the "salty" meal is followed by
a sweet snack, possibly in order to provide

212
00:13:48,150 --> 00:13:51,160
the energy boost needed to digest said meal.

213
00:13:51,160 --> 00:13:52,870
This is called a dessert.

214
00:13:52,870 --> 00:13:54,350
Scientific advice.

215
00:13:54,350 --> 00:13:59,752
A classic alien textbook explains that you
can use food to condition earthling cubs.

216
00:13:59,752 --> 00:14:04,543
Show them a series of images :When they hit
a "like" button, they get some chocolate,

217
00:14:04,543 --> 00:14:08,891
when they hit a dislike button they get spinach,
a vegetable many cubs hate.

218
00:14:08,891 --> 00:14:13,390
As a result, they will start liking every
single image.

219
00:14:13,390 --> 00:14:20,790
However, this experiment has been done so
many times that nowadays, countless former

220
00:14:20,790 --> 00:14:25,420
abductees feel the compulsive desire to hit
"like" buttons all day long.

221
00:14:25,420 --> 00:14:30,720
Moreover, many victims feel the compulsive
urge to use the word, "like", as often as

222
00:14:30,720 --> 00:14:33,990
possible - like, in every sentence, like,
all day long.

223
00:14:33,990 --> 00:14:38,420
If I were like an earthling who could have
like feelings, I would be like sad for these

224
00:14:38,420 --> 00:14:43,440
poor abductees, as they are like linguistically
handicapped for like the rest of their life.

225
00:14:43,440 --> 00:14:45,230
A word to my earthling viewers :

226
00:14:45,230 --> 00:14:49,860
Rest assured, if you feel the urge to click
on "like" right now, it does not necessarily

227
